# The docker build context is the REPO ROOT -- required so examples/<app>/mod.rs (the one and
# only copy of each example app's source) is reachable by enclave-server/Containerfile. This file
# is what stops that context from including the ~500 MB of frontend node_modules and the cargo
# target/ dir that also live under this root.
#
# NOTE: .dockerignore patterns are ANCHORED AT THE CONTEXT ROOT, not gitignore-style any-depth.
# `src` below means <root>/src (the Solidity sources) and does NOT touch enclave-server/src --
# which is a build input. Use **/ for any-depth matching.

# VCS + Foundry submodules (lib/ alone is ~17 MB of OpenZeppelin + forge-std)
.git
.gitmodules
.gitattributes
lib

# Solidity sources, Foundry config and Foundry build state -- not enclave build inputs
src
script
test
out
cache
broadcast
deployments
foundry.toml
foundry.lock
remappings.txt

# Frontends + node (web/ alone is hundreds of MB, almost all node_modules)
web
**/node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json
scripts
.bin-foundry

# Operator-side tooling and docs -- never build inputs
tools
*.md

# Local/operator state and generated artifacts. Mutable per-deploy state MUST be out of the
# context so it can never perturb a build.
.secrets
.work
.work-calldata
.claude
enclave-server/deployments
enclave-server/instances.json
enclave-server/out
**/target
enclave-server/src/nautilus-server/target
*.eif
*.pcrs
